<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Romania is a country in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, formed in the nineteenth century from the union of the principalities of Wallachia and Moldavia. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it was greatly enlarged with territories, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, taken from the dissolved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>. Its lands were earlier part of the cultural and religious sphere of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, as the Byzantine Empire profile notes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romania.jpg" alt="Romania" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AdiJapan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Romania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
